Our client is an established international organisation with its headquarters in Nivelles. As part of an important organisational transformation, the company is redesigning its Target Operating Model to strengthen collaboration, clarify responsibilities and establish more efficient and consistent ways of working across the Group.

As a Freelance Senior Project & Process Manager (TOM) your responsibilities are:

• Lead the planning, coordination and execution of TOM design and implementation activities across the Group ;
• Structure project workstreams, milestones, deliverables and implementation plans ;
• Monitor dependencies, risks and issues, ensuring progress and alignment with business priorities ;
• Coordinate stakeholders, facilitate project meetings and support decision-making ;
• Prepare management updates and ensure clear communication on project progress ;
• Translate agreed TOM deliverables into concrete actions and sustainable implementation ;
• Support change management and the adoption of new organisational practices ;


A successful Freelance Senior Project & Process Manager (TOM) should have:

• At least 8 years of experience in project management, business transformation, operational excellence, business process management or organisational design ;
• Proven track record in leading complex, cross-functional transformation projects ;
• Strong project management and stakeholder management capabilities ;
• Excellent knowledge of business process mapping, workflow analysis and structured documentation ;
• Ability to translate complex business activities into clear, practical processes and ways of working ;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the confidence to challenge existing practices constructively ;
• Fluent in French & English ;

• Conduct in-depth analyses of P&L, ROCE, and risk management for specific market segments, identifying trends and growth potential;
• Translate financial data into clear reports and presentations, providing strategic insights and recommendations;
• Optimize working capital and monitor key risks related to accumulated positions and essential raw materials;
• Manage the planning process, including periodic forecasts, annual budgeting, and strategic planning up to EBIT level;
• Contribute to key investment projects, including CAPEX and M&A, by providing financial expertise;
• Collaborate with the Reporting Factory to enhance reporting and analysis tools, ensuring consistency and accuracy;
• Act as a strong business partner by supporting market segments and facilitating strategic decisions with financial insights.

Must-haves:

• You hold a master’s degree in finance, business administration, or a related field;
• Acquire at least 4 years of experience in finance, preferably as a controller or business partner;
• Demonstrate strong analytical skills to translate financial data into strategic insights;
• Communicate fluently in Dutch, both written and spoken;
• Possess excellent communication skills to present complex financial concepts clearly;
• Collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and senior management.
Nice-to-haves:

• Have experience working with SAP or similar ERP systems.
• Speak English or French in addition to Dutch.
• Show a proactive mindset with a hands-on approach to problem-solving.
• Bring experience in investment analysis, CAPEX, or M&A.
• he Demonstrate tability to optimize working capital and risk management.

As a Key Account Manager, you will manage a portfolio of approximately 15 to 20 clients, primarily airlines and aircraft maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO) organisations.

Your role combines strategic account management, business development, B2B negotiation and regular international client visits.

Your main responsibilities will include:

•   
Managing, retaining and developing your existing client portfolio;

•   
Overseeing key accounts and strategic client relationships;

•   
Understanding clients' commercial, technical and operational challenges and proposing suitable solutions;

•   
Preparing commercial proposals, responding to tenders and negotiating contracts;

•   
Maintaining regular face-to-face contact with clients and prospects;

•   
Developing new business opportunities;

•   
Preparing sales forecasts and budgets for each client;

•   
Monitoring profitability, volumes and sales performance;

•   
Conducting market analysis and keeping up with developments in the aerospace sector;

•   
Representing the company at industry events and client meetings.

The role involves regular travel across the EMEA region, accounting for approximately 50% of working time, generally on short trips.

This opportunity may particularly appeal to Account Managers, Key Account Managers, Sales Account Managers or Business Development Managers with proven experience in managing strategic client relationships.


•   
You ideally hold a Master's degree in Business, Management or a related field.

•   
You have at least four years of B2B sales experience in an international industrial environment. Experience in the aerospace sector is an advantage.

•   
You have an excellent command of French and English, with C1-level English required. Knowledge of another language used in the EMEA region is an advantage, particularly Arabic.

You stand out through:

•   
A strong customer focus;

•   
Solid negotiation skills;

•   
Excellent interpersonal and presentation skills;

•   
A sound understanding of financial and commercial considerations;

•   
The ability to work in international and multicultural environments;

•   
Autonomy, analytical thinking and effective prioritisation;

•   
The ability to collaborate effectively with a range of internal teams.

WHAT WE OFFER

Working in a fast-paced, constantly evolving environment, you will provide excellent customer service and hands-on support. This is a great opportunity to join an ambitious company at the forefront of its industry and play a key role in delivering a high-quality IT support service.

This is a varied and challenging role. You will ensure that support requests and incidents are handled promptly and professionally. You should take a proactive approach, responding to queries by phone, email, and in person. You will also act as an escalation point, working with third-party resolver groups to address issues that you are unable to resolve yourself.
Job responsibilities
• Provide support that consistently meets or exceeds customer expectations;
• Identify, analyse, and repair product failures. Order and replace parts as needed;
• Support and maintain user account information, including rights, security, and system groups;
• Receive and resolve issues from Tiers 2 and 3 when on-site assistance is needed to solve a hardware or software issue, in cooperation with the resolver group that transferred the issue, if necessary;
• Provide troubleshooting and problem-resolution support for all network devices;
• Coordinate with third-party vendors to resolve hardware and software problems, as required;
• Receive and resolve hardware- or software-related issues from Tiers 2 and 3 when on-site break-fix support is needed;
• Work with hardware and software vendors on planning and problem resolution;
• Work with manufacturers and third-party vendors to obtain technical assistance;
• Install PCs, peripherals, and LAN-based equipment;
• Assist with setting up security, file access, and other administrative procedures related to office moves;
• Move workstations, peripherals, and telecommunications equipment, as required;
• Order, receive, and provide all required equipment, materials, and third-party vendor services to implement IMACs;
• Install and set up equipment, cables, outlets, and all other hardware required to implement IMACs;
• Test completed IMACs and confirm acceptance by the end user;
• Document changes to inventory use and configuration;
• Provide AV and conference support for software such as Webex, Skype for Business, and Zoom.

• At least 5 years' experience in onsite support. An equivalent combination of education and related experience may also serve to meet these minimum requirements;
• ITIL V4 Foundation Certification (recommended);
• Microsoft Operating System / Office Certification(s) will be an asset;
• Advanced MS Office 365 skills;
• Scripting, coding skill will be considered an advantage;
• Able to solve simple hardware issues;
• iOS, Android advanced user, Basic Networking skills;
• Knowledge of Active Directory, permissions;
• Team Player and Analytical Thinking;
• Open and positive personality and ability to manage stress effectively;
• Customer oriented (Service awareness) with good interpersonal and communication skills;
• Able to adapt in a fast-evolving technology environment and ability to learn;
• Able to assume day to day responsibilities generating specific deliverables;
• Relationship-builder, at ease with people and capable of quickly building trust;
• Language skills: Proficiency in Dutch and a good level of English.

• Book investment transactions executed on behalf of clients;  
• Check the consistency of booked transactions against information received from intermediaries and counterparties;  
• Monitor securities positions and cash movements related to transactions;  
• Perform reconciliations between internal data and bank/counterparty statements and confirmations, and identify any discrepancies;  
• Monitor the settlement of transactions and ensure that any discrepancies or exceptions are properly investigated and resolved;  
• Process and monitor corporate actions, including dividends, coupons, redemptions, stock splits, etc.;  
• Participate in the preparation and review of operational and financial reports for internal teams and/or clients;  
• Maintain client data and files in relation to transactions and contribute to data quality within our systems;  
• Collaborate with the Front Office, Finance, Compliance and Risk teams, as well as with banks and other external partners;  
• Contribute to the continuous improvement of Back Office processes, controls and procedures;  
• Work closely with the Belgian Back Office team   
Ad hoc responsibilities 

• Handle, redirect and follow up on incoming phone calls and emails;  
• Welcome visitors and provide reception support;  
• Prepare and follow up on client payment orders;  
• Carry out various organisational and administrative tasks, including updating procedures and preparing tax certificates, certificates of ownership, etc. 

• You have a relevant secondary or higher education qualification and experience in a similar role. Previous experience in the banking sector would be an advantage;  
• You are versatile, autonomous and proactive;  
• You have excellent command of MS Office;  
• You have strong organisational skills, a good sense of priorities and a keen eye for detail;  
• You have excellent written and verbal communication skills;  
• You are fluent in Dutch and English. Knowledge of French would be an advantage.

